---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Why Do My Bra Cups Gap? Causes & Solutions | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Discover why your bra cups gap or pucker at the top. Learn how cup volume, breast shape, molded styles, and scoop-and-swoop techniques fix cup gaping."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/fit-guide/bra-cup-gaping"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Fit Guide', url: '/fit-guide' },
      { label: 'Bra Cup Gaping' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Fit Diagnostic
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        Why Do My Bra Cups Gap?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Empty space, wrinkling, or puckering at the top of your bra cups is one of the most frustrating fit issues. Here is how to diagnose whether it is caused by cup volume or style mismatch.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <section class="bg-canvas-soft-2 border-2 border-primary/30 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">Quick Answer</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed font-medium mb-4">
          Bra cups gap when <strong>the cup volume is too large</strong>, when <strong>the bra style doesn't match your natural breast shape</strong>, or counter-intuitively, when a band is too tight pushing cups away from the body.
        </p>
        <div class="max-w-md mx-auto my-4">
          <img 
            src="/img/fit-cup-gaping.svg" 
            alt="Vector diagram demonstrating cup gaping and empty space at top of molded bra cup" 
            width="400" 
            height="240" 
            class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline" 
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <span class="text-center text-xs text-mute mt-2 block font-medium">Figure 1: Empty gap space at top of bra cup</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Possible Causes -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Plausible Causes</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">1. Cup Volume Is Too Large</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">If your breast tissue doesn't fill the cup capacity, fabric or foam will pucker at the apex or neckline.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">2. Molded Foam Cup Misalignment</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">Pre-shaped T-shirt bras hold a rigid form. If your natural breast root is teardrop or shallow-topped, stiff foam cups will gape at the top edge even if the volume is correct.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">3. Band Is Too Small (Orange in a Glass Effect)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">If a band or underwire is too narrow, your breast tissue cannot sink into the base of the cup, leaving empty space in the upper cup.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What to Check -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Practical Fit Checks</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li><strong>Scoop and Swoop:</strong> Lean forward, place your hand inside the cup, and pull side breast tissue forward from under your arm into the center of the cup.</li>
          <li><strong>Posture Test:</strong> Sit naturally and lean slightly back. If gaping occurs only when slouching, the bra style may be too tall for your torso.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- What Size Change Might Help -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Recommended Size Adjustment</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          If your scoop-and-swoop test still leaves empty cup space, try decreasing your cup letter by one size while keeping the band size identical:
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl text-center mb-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">CUP SIZE ADJUSTMENT</span>
          <p class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">If 34D gaps after swooping &rarr; Try a 34C cup</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Alternatively, try unlined stretch-lace plunge or balconette styles that conform to natural breast tissue.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Calculator CTA -->
      <section class="bg-primary text-white rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 text-center sm:text-left flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6 shadow-md">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-1">Calculate Your Baseline Size</h2>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-canvas-soft-2">Verify your measurements using our direct underbust sizing calculator.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/#calculator" class="flex-shrink-0 h-12 px-6 bg-surface hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm rounded-xl shadow-xs transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>Calculate My Size &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- Related Fit Guides -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Related Fit Guides</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold">
          <a href="/fit-guide/bra-spillage" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Are My Breasts Spilling Out of My Bra?</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide/underwire-digging" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Does My Bra Underwire Dig In?</a>
          <a href="/sister-size-calculator" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Sister Size Calculator</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Return to Fit Guide Hub</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
